course: dictionary
lesson: 1980
title: Who is a composer?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A composer is a person who writes music, such as songs, symphonies, operas or film music. The word tells you the job: a composer composes, which means makes up the music.
explain: Context helps here too. «Film music is usually written specially for the film by a composer.» The clue is written by: the composer is the one who writes the music you hear in a film.
explain: Names can be clues as well. «In the Kodaly method, named after the Hungarian composer Zoltan Kodaly» tells you that Zoltan Kodaly was a person who wrote music. Look for a name placed next to the word.
explain: You do not have to be famous to be a composer. Pupils become composers when they make up their own tunes, so if you invent a tune, you are composing.
fact: A composer is a person who writes music.
fact: Composers write songs, symphonies, operas and film music.
fact: Composers write music down in notation, or they can use computers to do it.
fact: Famous composers include Bach, Mozart, Beethoven, Clara Schumann, Florence Price and John Williams.
fact: «Composer» is a noun, and its plural is «composers».
exercise: «Film music is usually written specially for the film by a composer.» Who writes film music? | A cinema usher | A football referee | *A composer
exercise: «John Williams wrote the Jaws music in 1975.» What was John Williams? | *A composer | A ticket seller | A conductor who only waves a baton
exercise: Nadia says, «A composer only plays music on stage.» What is the truth about a composer? | A composer only sells instruments in a shop | *A composer writes music, such as songs or symphonies | A composer only plays music on stage
test: «Composers such as Bach, Handel and Vivaldi wrote music for the recorder.» Find and copy one word that means a person who writes music. | recorder | music | instrument | *composers
test: Pupils become composers when they do what? | *Make up their own tunes | Sit silently in a concert | Sell instruments in a shop
exam: Which sentence uses the word composer correctly? | The composer of the football match scored two goals | The composer sang the notes, so we all sat down to listen | We bought a composer from the music shop | *Mozart was a composer who wrote many symphonies
